      "raw_completion": "{ \"goal_restatement\": \"Determine the minimum number of squares that must be removed from a 7\u00d77 chessboard such that the remaining squares cannot form a domino.\",\n\"conditions_complete\": true,\n\"contradictory\": false,\n\"multiple_reasonable_interpretations\": false,\n\"solution_exists\": true,\n\"unique_or_explicit_grading\": true,\n\"label\": \"A\",\n\"confidence\": 0.95,\n\"probability_label_A\": 0.95,\n\"issue_types\": [],\n\"reasoning_summary\": \"The problem requires finding the minimum number of squares to remove from a 7\u00d77 chessboard so that the remaining squares cannot form a domino. A domino covers two adjacent squares, either horizontally or vertically. To prevent the formation of a domino, we need to ensure that no two adjacent squares remain. The most efficient way to do this is to remove all squares of one color (since a domino always covers one black and one white square on a chessboard). A 7\u00d77 chessboard has 25 squares of one color and 24 of the other. Therefore, removing 25 squares will ensure that no two adjacent squares remain, preventing the formation of a domino.\",\n\"derived_answer\":   \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \